**Fabric-hostable rule (operator-signed):** a service is fabric-hostable when it is expressible as **immutable storage + stateless compute + explicit route + read-back receipt**; anything requiring local mutable state is not fabric-portable until its state moves into a \`StorageBinding\`. "Connect the right users to the right resources" is the fabric's future value, not active work: \`RoutePolicy\` (nearest/cheapest/least-loaded/trust), multi-replica routes, cert/DNS automation land later, when they hurt — the first version connects ONE domain to ONE admitted allocation and proves it did.

